  "minimum_rule": "A run measures speed only if the GPU is busy long enough and evenly enough. Two rules, the larger wins: (1) at least 1 s of photons, so that the launch and the clock's ramp-up don't dominate; (2) at least 32 chunks per resident thread, so that every SM gets a fair share and the slowest one doesn't decide the time (at 10\u2077 photons on the laptop: 9 766 chunks for ~28 800 threads, and pass times varied 0.6\u20131.6\u00d7; research/pass_order.py)."
